&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Rolling Chairs&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if patient meets Mobility Assistive Equipment clinical criteria (see &amp;sect;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=219&amp;ncdver=2&amp;DocID=280.3&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;280.3&lt;&sol;a&gt; of the NCD Manual). Coverage is limited to those roll-about chairs having casters of at least 5 inches in diameter and specifically designed to meet the needs of ill, injured, or otherwise impaired individuals.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; Coverage is denied for the wide range of chairs with smaller casters as are found in general use in homes, offices, and institutions for many purposes not related to the care&sol;treatment of ill&sol;injured persons. This type is not primarily medical in nature. (&amp;sect;1861(n) of the Act.)&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Safety Rollers&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if patient meets Mobility Assistive Equipment clinical criteria (see &amp;sect;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=219&amp;ncdver=2&amp;DocID=280.3&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;280.3&lt;&sol;a&gt; of this manual).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Sauna Baths&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Deny - not primarily medical in nature; personal comfort items (&amp;sect;&amp;sect;1861(n) and 1862(a)(6) of the Act).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Seat Elevation Equipment (power-operated) on Medicare Covered Power Wheelchairs&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; DME on Medicare-covered power wheelchairs, and covered under conditions specified in &amp;sect;280.16 of this manual.&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Seat Lifts&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered under the conditions specified in &amp;sect;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=221&amp;ncdver=1&amp;DocID=280.4&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;280.4&lt;&sol;a&gt; of this manual.  Refer all to medical staff for this determination.&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  &lt;a name=&quot;scpm&quot; id=&quot;scpm&quot;&gt;&lt;&sol;a&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;scpm&quot; id=&quot;scpm&quot;&gt;&lt;&sol;a&gt;Self Contained Pacemaker Monitors&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered when prescribed by a physician for a patient with a cardiac pacemaker. (See &amp;sect;&amp;sect;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=160&amp;ncdver=1&amp;DocID=20.8.1&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;20.8.1&lt;&sol;a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=168&amp;ncdver=1&amp;DocID=280.2&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;280.2&lt;&sol;a&gt; of this manual.)&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Sitz Baths&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if MAC&#39;s medical staff determines patient has an infection or injury of the perineal area and the item has been prescribed by the patient&amp;#8217;s physician as a part of his planned regimen of treatment in the patient&amp;#8217;s home.&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Spare Tanks of Oxygen&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Deny - convenience or precautionary supply.&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Speech Teaching Machines&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Deny - education equipment; not primarily medical in nature (&amp;sect;1861(n) of the Act).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Stairway Elevators&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Deny - (See &lt;a href=&quot;#elevator&quot;&gt;Elevators&lt;&sol;a&gt;.) (&amp;sect;1861(n) of the Act).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Standing Tables&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Deny - convenience item; not primarily medical in nature (&amp;sect;1861(n) of the Act).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Steam Packs&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; These packs are Covered under the same conditions as heating pads.  (See &lt;a href=&quot;#hp&quot;&gt;Heating Pads&lt;&sol;a&gt;.)&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Suction Machines&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if MAC&#39;s medical staff determines that the machine specified in the claim is medically required and appropriate for home use without technical or professional supervision.&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Support Hose&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Deny - (See &lt;a href=&quot;#fabric&quot;&gt;Fabric Supports&lt;&sol;a&gt;.) (&amp;sect;1861(n) of the Act).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Surgical Leggings&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Deny - non-reusable supply; not rental-type item (&amp;sect;1861(n) of the Act).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Telephone Alert Systems&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Deny - these are emergency communications systems and do not serve a diagnostic or therapeutic purpose.&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  &lt;a name=&quot;ts&quot; id=&quot;ts&quot;&gt;Toilet Seats&lt;&sol;a&gt;&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Deny - not medical equipment (&amp;sect;1861(n) of the Act).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Traction Equipment&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if patient has orthopedic impairment requiring traction equipment that prevents ambulation during the period of use (Consider covering devices usable during ambulation; e.g., cervical traction collar, under the brace provision).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Trapeze Bars&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if patient is bed confined and the patient needs a trapeze bar to sit up because of respiratory condition, to change body position for other medical reasons, or to get in and out of bed.&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Treadmill&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Deny - exercise equipment; not primarily medical in nature (&amp;sect;1861(n) of the Act).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Ultraviolet Cabinets&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered for selected patients with generalized intractable psoriasis.  Using appropriate consultation, the MAC should determine whether medical and other factors justify treatment at home rather than at alternative sites, e.g., outpatient department of a hospital.&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Urinals autoclavable&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if patient is bed confined (hospital type).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Vaporizers&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if patient has a respiratory illness.&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  &lt;a name=&quot;vent&quot; id=&quot;vent&quot;&gt;Ventilators&lt;&sol;a&gt;&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered for treatment of neuromuscular diseases, thoracic restrictive diseases, and chronic respiratory failure consequent to chronic obstructive pulmonary disease &lt;font color=&quot;FF0000&quot;&gt;(See &amp;sect;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;view&sol;ncd.aspx?ncdid=380&amp;ncdver=1&amp;chapter=all&amp;labOnly=allncd&amp;sortBy=title&amp;bc=18&quot;&gt;240.9&lt;&sol;a&gt; of this manual.)&lt;&sol;font&gt;.  Includes both positive and negative pressure types. (See &amp;sect;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;view&sol;ncd.aspx?ncdid=229&amp;ncdver=1&amp;chapter=240&amp;labOnly=allncd&amp;sortBy=chapter&amp;bc=18&quot;&gt;240.5&lt;&sol;a&gt; of this manual.)&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;   

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Walkers&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if patient meets Mobility Assistive Equipment clinical criteria (see &amp;sect;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=219&amp;ncdver=2&amp;DocID=280.3&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;280.3&lt;&sol;a&gt; of this manual).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Water and Pressure Pads and Mattresses&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; (See &lt;a href=&quot;#appm&quot;&gt;Alternating Pressure Pads, Mattresses and Lamb&#39;s Wool Pads&lt;&sol;a&gt;.)&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Wheelchairs (manual)&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if patient meets Mobility Assistive Equipment clinical criteria (see &amp;sect;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=219&amp;ncdver=2&amp;DocID=280.3&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;280.3&lt;&sol;a&gt; of this manual).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Wheelchairs (power operated)&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if patient meets Mobility Assistive Equipment clinical criteria (see &amp;sect;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=219&amp;ncdver=2&amp;DocID=280.3&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;280.3&lt;&sol;a&gt; of this manual).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Wheelchairs (scooter&sol;POV)&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if patient meets Mobility Assistive Equipment clinical criteria (see &amp;sect;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=219&amp;ncdver=2&amp;DocID=280.3&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;280.3&lt;&sol;a&gt; of this manual).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Wheelchairs (specially-sized)&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if patient meets Mobility Assistive Equipment clinical criteria (see &amp;sect;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=219&amp;ncdver=2&amp;DocID=280.3&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;280.3&lt;&sol;a&gt; of this manual).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Whirlpool Bath Equipment&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Covered if patient is homebound and has a (standard)condition for which the whirlpool bath can be expected to provide substantial therapeutic benefit justifying its cost.  Where patient is not homebound but has such a condition, payment is restricted to the cost of providing the services elsewhere; e.g., an outpatient department of a participating hospital, if that alternative is less costly. In all cases, refer claim to medical staff for a determination.&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  Whirlpool Pumps&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Deny - (See &lt;a href=&quot;#pwp&quot;&gt;Portable Whirlpool Pumps&lt;&sol;a&gt;.) (&amp;sect;1861(n) of the Act).&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;

&lt;tr valign=&quot;top&quot;&gt;   
&lt;td scope=&quot;row&quot;&gt;  White Canes&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;td&gt; Deny - (See &amp;sect;&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=168&amp;ncdver=1&amp;DocID=280.2&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;280.2&lt;&sol;a&gt; of this manual.) (Not considered Mobility Assistive Equipment)&lt;&sol;td&gt;
&lt;&sol;tr&gt;
&lt;&sol;tbody&gt;
&lt;&sol;table&gt;
